    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96797470?u=46c8c541c2bd8c86ac9640e08df5c83009d14aff&v=4",
                "login": "TanbirRamim",
                "resourcePath": "/TanbirRamim",
                "url": "https://github.com/TanbirRamim"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "`parametrize` does this. put the tests in a set parametrized by the function name and every case inside runs once per entry, getting it as an argument:\n\n```lua\nT['impl'] = MiniTest.new_set({ parametrize = { { 'func_re' }, { 'func_ts' } } })\n\nT['impl']['returns the thing'] = function(fname)\n  local ret = child.lua('return ' .. fname .. '()')\n  eq(ret, expected)\nend\n```\n\nworks for nested sets too, everything under `T['impl']` gets multiplied. there's a small example under `:h MiniTest.new_set()`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">parametrize</code> does this. put the tests in a set parametrized by the function name and every case inside runs once per entry, getting it as an argument:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"T['impl'] = MiniTest.new_set({ parametrize = { { 'func_re' }, { 'func_ts' } } })\n\nT['impl']['returns the thing'] = function(fname)\n  local ret = child.lua('return ' .. fname .. '()')\n  eq(ret, expected)\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">T</span>[<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>impl<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniTest</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">new_set</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">parametrize</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>func_re<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}, { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>func_ts<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>} } })\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">T</span>[<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>impl<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>][<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>returns the thing<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">fname</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">ret</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">child</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">lua</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>return <span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">fname</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">eq</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">ret</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">expected</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">works for nested sets too, everything under <code class=\"notranslate\">T['impl']</code> gets multiplied. there's a small example under <code class=\"notranslate\">:h MiniTest.new_set()</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "parametrize does this. put the tests in a set parametrized by the function name and every case inside runs once per entry, getting it as an argument:\nT['impl'] = MiniTest.new_set({ parametrize = { { 'func_re' }, { 'func_ts' } } })\n\nT['impl']['returns the thing'] = function(fname)\n  local ret = child.lua('return ' .. fname .. '()')\n  eq(ret, expected)\nend\nworks for nested sets too, everything under T['impl'] gets multiplied. there's a small example under :h MiniTest.new_set().",
